module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_refusal_reason_and_its_class_are_paired_by_hand

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { AtCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyImpossible }

// A REFUSAL CARRIES TWO FACTS THAT MUST AGREE, AND THE TYPE LETS THEM DISAGREE. The reason names which
// decision answered no; the class says what kind of refusal that is, and it decides which diagnostic an
// author is shown. A record that takes both as independent fields pairs them at every construction site,
// and a wrong pair is a well-typed value.
data a_refusal_reason_and_its_class_are_paired_by_hand: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_refusal_reason_and_its_class_are_paired_by_hand" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: AtCeiling { rung: StructurallyImpossible, ceiling_reason: "structurally impossible at this head: InhabitanceRefused carries ONE InhabitanceRefusalReason value whose arm IS the class, so a reason from one family beside a class from another has no value to write, and every consumer -- production and claim -- matches the arm rather than re-pairing two fields. What is NOT closed is evidence: the claim rows that pin those arms are not compiled by required CI (gunbc.rung_drop), so the re-pinned rows still need the authorized claim run this namespace owes." } },

  receipts: [
    "**a pair of fields that must agree, with nothing making them agree, is one fact with many producers.** gunbc.design_argument::single_authority: one fact decided in more than one place is a fork, and the fact here is what kind of refusal this is -- produced at each construction site instead of read from the decision that made it. gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed asks that a wrong answer be unwritable, or typed, located and countable; a mismatched pair is neither, because it is just a value.",

    "INVALID STATE, THE VIOLATED INVARIANT, as it stood at ffd4e4ec: one decision answered no and the verdict it returned carried find_witness_reason: Symbol and refusal_class: InhabitanceRefusalClass as two independent fields (the InhabitanceRefused arm of InhabitanceVerdict, src/v2/std/inhabitance.dag). The invariant is that a reason and its class name the same decision. Nothing in the type enforced it: ^inhabitance_comparison_candidate_malformed beside RefusalStructuralMismatch was a well-typed value, and so was any other mismatch. That shape no longer exists at the head this row stands on.",

    "EVERY SITE THAT PAIRS, at the head this row is written on. Hand-written pairs, three, all in src/v2/std/inhabitance.dag: declared_type_inhabitance (an Optional produced where a required value is declared), inhabitance_optional_layer_verdict (the malformed-wrapper answer), and inhabitance_optional_layer_depth_mismatch_refusal (the depth-mismatch refusal, which the OptionalLayerDepthMismatch arm of inhabitance_optional_layer_verdict and the Absent arm of declared_type_inhabitance_optional now share). Sites that FORWARD a class decided elsewhere, two, both in the same module: declared_type_inhabitance_refusal and inhabitance_decision_through_argument, each taking refusal_class from an InhabitanceStructuralDecision. And the ONE classifier over the structural family, inhabitance_structural_decision, exhaustive with no default arm. Before this row's fix commit the hand-written count was four -- three inside declared_type_inhabitance and one inside inhabitance_with_payloads -- and two of them named the same fact twice. AT THE HEAD THIS ROW STANDS ON THERE IS NO PAIR LEFT TO GET WRONG: the three hand-written constructions build an arm of InhabitanceRefusalReason, the two forwarders carry one reason value, the classifier names the family once per arm, and every consumer -- src/v2/compiler/infer.dag and the claim modules that match InhabitanceRefused -- matches the arm instead of re-pairing two fields. That is the guarantee, not the mitigation.",

    "HARM AND CONSEQUENCE: the class is not decoration. inhabitance_refusal_diagnostic sends RefusalStructuralMismatch and RefusalWitnessSearchDecision to application_argument_does_not_inhabit_diagnostic, which carries a SUGGESTED NODE, and RefusalComparisonCouldNotRun to inhabitance_refusal_without_suggestion_diagnostic, which carries none. A mismatched pair therefore sends an author to fix a type error the compiler never showed. The cost of staying below the ceiling is that the next reason added at a new site can be paired with the wrong class and nothing refuses it -- which is not hypothetical, see the SPECIMEN.",

    "SPECIMEN, review 92072 at ffd4e4ec: the malformed-optional-wrapper arm paired ^inhabitance_optional_layer_wrapper_malformed with RefusalStructuralMismatch, while the classifier in the same module puts every malformed input in RefusalComparisonCouldNotRun and describes that family as never a claim that the value's type is wrong. A malformed occupancy wrapper is an input that is not a well-formed node, so the shipped pair contradicted its own module, and the author-facing diagnostic offered a suggested fix for a type error that did not exist. The fix commit this row is written on decides the class once, inside the layer judgement, and shares one construction between the two depth-mismatch routes. Its discriminators are v2.test.claim.compiler.optional_layers a_malformed_occupancy_wrapper_refuses_as_could_not_run and a_malformed_occupancy_wrapper_diagnostic_carries_no_suggested_node, with a_depth_mismatch_keeps_the_type_mismatch_class_and_its_suggestion and an_optional_at_a_required_declared_position_keeps_the_type_mismatch_class as controls. Those five rows are re-pinned against the closed sum at this head and they remain UNEXECUTED: required CI does not compile claim modules (gunbc.rung_drop), and the authorized paired claim run this PR asks for is what turns them from readings of the type into readings of behaviour.",

    "PRESENT RUNG: at ceiling -- structurally impossible for this pair. The class IS the arm of InhabitanceRefusalReason = RefusalReasonStructuralMismatch { reason } | RefusalReasonComparisonCouldNotRun { reason } | RefusalReasonWitnessSearchDecision { reason }; InhabitanceRefused carries { reason: InhabitanceRefusalReason, position }; refusal_class is deleted and read from the arm, so a mismatched pair has no constructor and no site can re-pair the two facts. The classifier over the structural family stays exhaustive with no default arm, which is what makes a new comparison arm name its family instead of inheriting one. WHAT THAT RUNG DOES NOT CLAIM: a closed shape says nothing about behaviour. The claim rows that pin these arms are still not compiled by required CI (gunbc.rung_drop), and the authorized paired run over them is owed.",

    "ACCOUNTABLE OWNER: session valiant-deer-27, managed by tidy-ant-251, on gunb-ai/gunbc#15868; the closed-sum migration this row used to defer was landed inside that PR, by session lively-crane-453, on the integration manager's decision after review 92373 item 3 and review 92403. A named session and a named PR, so the work belongs to someone. The row stays here rather than in a PR description because the PR closes the day and this row outlives it. It does not read as closed on the strength of the type alone: the shape is closed, the evidence for the re-pinned claim rows is not, and the next change that touches a refusal must read this row together with the run it still owes.",

    "CAPABILITY TRIGGER, named as a capability and not as a date: the claim-site consumers that match InhabitanceRefused must be COMPILED under an authorized route, and EXECUTED where behavioural evidence is required. Required CI alone does not do that -- the v2-bootstrap job compiles the production closures and omits the claim modules (gunbc.rung_drop). The first half of the trigger was met while this PR was open: the granted claim batch (claim_batch --hermetic, roots dag and src/v2, run for gunb-ai/gunbc#15363) compiles claim closures and reports their type errors, which is how a value-does-not-inhabit diagnostic in another namespace's claim module was caught. So the migration was landed inside this change instead of beside it; the execution half is still owed and is the paired run this PR asks for.",

    "MIGRATION, where it landed and what it re-pinned: the ceiling shape was landed in gunb-ai/gunbc#15868 itself. The claim-site census was re-derived at this head (src/v2/test/claim/compiler/optional_layers.dag, infer_optional_at_required_witness, infer_declared_return_inhabitance_witness, infer_sibling_position_inhabitance_witness, infer_application_argument_inhabitance_witness, free_semigroup_empty_producer_witness, src/v2/test/claim/std/inhabitance_argument_path_order_witness) and every refusal row now names the arm it expects instead of a reason and a class. Outstanding, and tracked rather than implied: the authorized paired claim run over those modules at this head, against merge base 209644f4, which is what turns the re-pinned rows from readings of the type into readings of behaviour.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
